  "id": "DrugBank_DB00515 - MONDO_20542",
  "verbalization": "Cisplatin is implicated in the development of Malignant Sertoli-leydig Cell Tumor Of Ovary through a pathway involving Altretamine, which is linked to both Familial Ovarian Cancer and Immature Ovarian Teratoma. The evidence suggests that Cisplatin may exert a therapeutic or pathogenic effect on these tumors, as it is associated with multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the malignant Sertoli-leydig cell tumor. The presence of Altretamine as a common intermediate in these pathways indicates a potential mechanism by which Cisplatin could influence the progression or manifestation of the tumor. The overlapping indications and the shared role of Altretamine suggest a possible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
